      "layout": "Q",
      "strengths": "Like P, it presents the three identification columns completely at first sight, keeps headers on one line, and limits measured word breaks to two. Its wider purity column provides a little more breathing room.",
      "faults": "The extra purity width does not change the visible line pattern or row heights relative to P. The longest name still wraps, and purity and storage require scrolling.",
      "spatial_logic": "It follows P's identification-first arrangement but adds 9 px to purity, increasing total scroll distance without an evident improvement in the render."
    },
    {
      "layout": "R",
      "strengths": "Names, formulas and CAS numbers remain visible together initially. Its narrower storage column makes the table somewhat shorter horizontally, and the even row heights create a regular grid.",
      "faults": "The storage text has eight measured word breaks, including an awkward separation of a temperature from its unit. Every data row reaches three lines, increasing height compared with P and Q; the wider purity column does not visibly make its entries more compact.",
