  "insights": "The scrolling layouts preserve chemical identifiers far better than the fitted layouts. P and Q make an especially useful initial lookup view because the first three columns fit together; T improves the longest name but loses a complete CAS number at first sight. The storage prose largely determines row height, so extra width in short fields can create empty space without shortening the table. In a 360 px fitted grid there is no allocation that can keep the 135 px formula, 78 px CAS entry and long storage prose comfortably whole after padding; the fitted design must choose which reading task to protect. Proposed widths are hypotheses and need rendered verification, especially for line breaks and the exact viewport boundary.",
